1
00:00:00,106 --> 00:00:01,371
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,373 --> 00:00:02,940
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,446 --> 00:00:04,576
(Episode 14)

4
00:00:04,601 --> 00:00:05,601
Honey.

5
00:00:06,190 --> 00:00:07,337
K-Montessori?

6
00:00:07,679 --> 00:00:08,679
Yeah.

7
00:00:09,192 --> 00:00:11,772
You keep saying I never tell you anything,
so I'm telling you now.

8
00:00:11,797 --> 00:00:13,442
I'm officially reporting to you, Madam.

9
00:00:13,445 --> 00:00:14,445
My lifelong dream...

10
00:00:14,555 --> 00:00:16,504
is to publish books for adults first,

11
00:00:16,528 --> 00:00:20,065
then create animated stories
for the next generation.

12
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:23,259
I thought you'd run a publishing house
for a few years, then enter politics.

13
00:00:23,318 --> 00:00:25,023
I told you I'd never go into politics.

14
00:00:25,148 --> 00:00:26,831
Why are you so determined not to?

15
00:00:26,856 --> 00:00:28,551
Most people would jump at the opportunity.

16
00:00:28,744 --> 00:00:31,514
Sun Kyung, give him a chance
to explain his plan.

17
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:33,362
Thanks, little brother.

18
00:00:34,370 --> 00:00:35,508
It's just as I said.

19
00:00:35,532 --> 00:00:38,978
Lieutenant No is looking for staff
and has contacted headhunters too.

20
00:00:39,768 --> 00:00:42,062
I think I know someone
who can be recommended.

21
00:00:42,087 --> 00:00:43,876
- Really? Who?
- One of my friends.

22
00:00:43,932 --> 00:00:45,246
He's running a café right now.

23
00:00:46,071 --> 00:00:48,658
You know him, Mom.
Geum Tae O from kindergarten.

24
00:00:48,905 --> 00:00:49,905
Geum Tae O.

25
00:00:50,332 --> 00:00:51,844
Geum Tae O, from the tuna factory family.

26
00:00:52,098 --> 00:00:53,725
His family runs a large tuna factory.

27
00:00:55,545 --> 00:00:59,175
I remember him
because his last name is Geum, not Kim.

28
00:00:59,315 --> 00:01:01,055
Really? Then let's meet him.

29
00:01:01,125 --> 00:01:02,166
Okay.

30
00:01:02,191 --> 00:01:03,732
He's trying to raise some money.

31
00:01:04,452 --> 00:01:05,505
He's looking for investors.

32
00:01:06,418 --> 00:01:08,484
Good thing you brought him up.

33
00:01:42,925 --> 00:01:46,890
I'm sorry. I'll find a way
to stop the lawsuit.

34
00:01:48,538 --> 00:01:49,700
(Jeong Won)

35
00:01:55,725 --> 00:01:56,725
It's me.

36
00:01:57,157 --> 00:01:59,626
You're the woman seeing Seung Woo, right?

37
00:02:00,132 --> 00:02:01,402
You shameless bitch.

38
00:02:01,792 --> 00:02:03,729
After ruining someone's life like that...

39
00:02:03,852 --> 00:02:04,887
Where are you?

40
00:02:04,912 --> 00:02:06,319
We need to meet.

41
00:02:07,551 --> 00:02:08,866
Mom, what are you doing?

42
00:02:10,719 --> 00:02:12,091
I'll call you later.

43
00:02:14,312 --> 00:02:16,105
Why did you look through my phone?

44
00:02:16,152 --> 00:02:17,428
There was something worth seeing.

45
00:02:17,452 --> 00:02:18,993
What? You think I'm a stranger?

46
00:02:19,017 --> 00:02:21,094
- Mom.
- You still haven't broken up with her?

47
00:02:21,119 --> 00:02:22,734
You still haven't come to your senses.

48
00:02:23,325 --> 00:02:25,412
What else has to happen
before you finally wake up?

49
00:02:25,415 --> 00:02:26,633
What is she to you?

50
00:02:26,658 --> 00:02:28,151
What does that crazy bitch mean to you?

51
00:02:28,154 --> 00:02:29,425
Don't insult her!

52
00:02:30,585 --> 00:02:32,178
She's the woman I loved.

53
00:02:32,202 --> 00:02:33,409
Cha Seung Woo.

54
00:02:33,864 --> 00:02:35,205
You crazy fool.

55
00:02:35,258 --> 00:02:37,491
After everything you've been through,

56
00:02:37,516 --> 00:02:38,644
you still say you love her?

57
00:02:38,669 --> 00:02:40,818
- Can't you come to your senses? Get out!
- Mom.

58
00:02:40,842 --> 00:02:42,405
Get out!

59
00:02:43,865 --> 00:02:45,712
You crazy fool.

60
00:02:51,824 --> 00:02:53,017
Your mother too?

61
00:02:53,115 --> 00:02:54,211
Yes.

62
00:02:54,654 --> 00:02:57,587
The director must feel bad
about rejecting you.

63
00:02:57,612 --> 00:02:59,621
He even asked me and Tae O...

64
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:01,287
what happened between you and Do Hee.

65
00:03:01,312 --> 00:03:03,074
- Really?
- Yeah.

66
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:10,648
Where's Tae O?

67
00:03:11,123 --> 00:03:14,346
He's speaking with a customer right now.

68
00:03:14,722 --> 00:03:15,889
I'll go get him.

69
00:03:15,913 --> 00:03:17,413
Thank you.

70
00:03:24,556 --> 00:03:27,269
I heard you asked my mom some questions.

71
00:03:27,838 --> 00:03:30,555
I'm not planning to apply
to the Art and Culture Center,

72
00:03:30,923 --> 00:03:32,540
so please don't feel pressured.

73
00:03:32,564 --> 00:03:33,996
I really liked your paintings.

74
00:03:34,341 --> 00:03:35,939
To be honest,
that's why I was concerned...

75
00:03:36,158 --> 00:03:37,215
about you.

76
00:03:38,247 --> 00:03:39,428
Thank you.

77
00:03:40,305 --> 00:03:41,447
But...

78
00:03:42,940 --> 00:03:44,830
you didn't look into things properly,

79
00:03:44,854 --> 00:03:46,825
and rejected me based on what you saw.

80
00:03:46,827 --> 00:03:48,198
And now you're doing all this.

81
00:03:48,305 --> 00:03:51,374
Honestly, it's ridiculous and off-putting.

82
00:03:52,605 --> 00:03:54,419
I understand why you'd say that, but...

83
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:56,946
if you came in with rumors like those,

84
00:03:56,990 --> 00:03:58,706
you couldn't have focused on your art.

85
00:04:00,072 --> 00:04:02,921
How can you lead a division
with such poor judgment?

86
00:04:02,992 --> 00:04:05,662
You only saw me being harsh with Do Hee.

87
00:04:05,945 --> 00:04:09,969
You rejected me without checking
what led up to it or asking me.

88
00:04:10,568 --> 00:04:12,690
You just heard what others said about me.

89
00:04:14,012 --> 00:04:15,474
And not out of concern for me, either.

90
00:04:15,476 --> 00:04:17,853
You were worried
that you'd made the wrong decision.

91
00:04:17,925 --> 00:04:19,427
You even called my mother in.

92
00:04:19,558 --> 00:04:20,570
Isn't that true?

93
00:04:21,002 --> 00:04:22,882
Yes. I admit it.

94
00:04:22,938 --> 00:04:26,768
If you make judgments
based on a single moment,

95
00:04:26,811 --> 00:04:29,388
you'll end up regretting it a lot.

96
00:04:29,413 --> 00:04:31,378
Just a word of advice.

97
00:04:32,968 --> 00:04:34,880
I believe I understand your point.

98
00:04:37,101 --> 00:04:38,337
But,

99
00:04:38,924 --> 00:04:40,428
you should be more careful.

100
00:04:40,492 --> 00:04:42,739
I heard you were throwing trash
during a fight.

101
00:04:42,764 --> 00:04:44,932
You heard all the details.

102
00:04:44,957 --> 00:04:46,949
Your hands are your livelihood.
You need to protect them.

103
00:04:47,218 --> 00:04:48,847
Find a safer way to exercise.

104
00:04:48,872 --> 00:04:51,235
You could go running in the morning.
There are plenty of options.

105
00:04:51,732 --> 00:04:53,657
This is all thanks to Do Hee,

106
00:04:54,145 --> 00:04:56,075
but I guess my mom didn't tell you.

107
00:04:58,537 --> 00:05:00,813
Your mother didn't say much.

108
00:05:02,159 --> 00:05:05,284
I didn't realize it had reached the point
where you had to learn this.

109
00:05:06,535 --> 00:05:08,411
Anyway, thank you for your concern.

110
00:05:08,978 --> 00:05:11,059
I'll decide how I exercise.

111
00:05:13,809 --> 00:05:15,062
What a cutie.

112
00:05:16,705 --> 00:05:19,695
You're finally smiling again, O Reum.

113
00:05:19,719 --> 00:05:21,452
Thank you.

114
00:05:22,115 --> 00:05:23,936
- Mom.
- Mom's here.

115
00:05:23,961 --> 00:05:24,962
Yes? What is it?

116
00:05:24,987 --> 00:05:27,257
O Reum hasn't felt this good in a while.

117
00:05:27,282 --> 00:05:29,050
The medicine seems to be working.

118
00:05:33,765 --> 00:05:35,158
O Reum...

119
00:05:35,885 --> 00:05:39,402
They think O Reum is seriously ill.

120
00:05:39,858 --> 00:05:41,367
What are you talking about?

121
00:05:42,305 --> 00:05:44,462
They want to do a bone marrow test.

122
00:05:45,199 --> 00:05:47,387
Mother, I'm scared.

123
00:05:48,251 --> 00:05:50,318
It might be a serious illness.

124
00:05:50,398 --> 00:05:51,398
What?

125
00:05:52,265 --> 00:05:55,212
What on earth are you talking about?

126
00:05:57,697 --> 00:06:01,458
What is my daughter-in-law talking about?

127
00:06:01,618 --> 00:06:04,592
She's a foreigner,
so she may have misunderstood.

128
00:06:04,617 --> 00:06:06,537
Was that child Cha O Reum?

129
00:06:06,561 --> 00:06:07,743
I'm his grandmother.

130
00:06:07,768 --> 00:06:10,215
His cold wasn't getting any better,

131
00:06:10,269 --> 00:06:12,044
so we came to change his medicine.

132
00:06:12,731 --> 00:06:15,228
First, you did a blood test,

133
00:06:15,907 --> 00:06:18,864
and now you want a bone marrow test. Why?

134
00:06:18,917 --> 00:06:20,290
Please sit down.

135
00:06:27,572 --> 00:06:30,001
His blood test results aren't very good.

136
00:06:30,012 --> 00:06:32,155
What does that mean?

137
00:06:32,251 --> 00:06:34,906
We suspect he may have blood cancer.

138
00:06:36,305 --> 00:06:38,951
- What?
- To be certain,

139
00:06:38,976 --> 00:06:42,101
I told his mother we'd need
to perform a bone marrow test.

140
00:06:42,639 --> 00:06:43,997
Admit him immediately.

141
00:06:46,185 --> 00:06:47,185
Ma'am?

142
00:06:49,569 --> 00:06:50,577
Yes.

143
00:06:51,882 --> 00:06:54,044
I understand.

144
00:06:54,986 --> 00:06:56,255
We'll do that.

145
00:06:56,299 --> 00:06:57,299
Of course.

146
00:07:00,218 --> 00:07:01,462
Ma'am.

147
00:07:15,225 --> 00:07:17,538
Mother, what did the doctor say?

148
00:07:17,607 --> 00:07:19,696
He needs to stay in the hospital, right?

149
00:07:20,505 --> 00:07:22,559
I understood correctly, right?

150
00:07:23,718 --> 00:07:25,384
Please, O Reum.

151
00:07:25,494 --> 00:07:28,058
My baby, please.

152
00:07:30,178 --> 00:07:31,907
Mother...

153
00:07:40,272 --> 00:07:41,480
It's okay.

154
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:43,150
It's probably nothing.

155
00:07:43,486 --> 00:07:44,772
Don't jump to conclusions.

156
00:07:44,797 --> 00:07:47,027
That's your worst habit.
Let's focus on the surgery first.

157
00:07:47,061 --> 00:07:49,249
We need to get O Reum
better as soon as possible.

158
00:07:50,172 --> 00:07:52,817
Can you handle the admission paperwork?

159
00:07:52,841 --> 00:07:53,890
Should I do it?

160
00:07:55,377 --> 00:07:57,010
I called Seung Hyun.

161
00:07:58,660 --> 00:07:59,660
Okay.

162
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:09,660
(Pediatrics)

163
00:08:13,906 --> 00:08:14,906
O Reum.

164
00:08:15,159 --> 00:08:16,549
Where's O Reum?

165
00:08:24,933 --> 00:08:25,933
What?

166
00:08:28,025 --> 00:08:30,254
Na Ji Ni, please come in.

167
00:08:30,278 --> 00:08:31,278
Okay.

168
00:08:31,983 --> 00:08:34,828
O Reum!

169
00:08:41,965 --> 00:08:43,074
Seung Hyun.

170
00:08:43,326 --> 00:08:45,206
What's going on? A bone marrow test?

171
00:08:45,231 --> 00:08:47,593
I'll explain later.
Get him admitted first.

172
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:48,640
Mom.

173
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:05,292
(Registration, Billing)

174
00:09:10,201 --> 00:09:11,953
O Reum, it can't be...

175
00:09:11,956 --> 00:09:13,991
- O Reum, it can't be true, right?
- Right.

176
00:09:14,604 --> 00:09:16,213
I'll trust you.

177
00:09:20,231 --> 00:09:22,278
You're so precious.

178
00:09:28,905 --> 00:09:32,384
Dad, where are we? Why am I wearing this?

179
00:09:32,544 --> 00:09:36,784
- You don't like it?
- No, I do. You should wear one too.

180
00:09:37,592 --> 00:09:39,092
They don't have one for me.

181
00:09:39,572 --> 00:09:41,167
Maybe I'm too tall.

182
00:09:41,191 --> 00:09:42,924
Beanpole.

183
00:09:45,752 --> 00:09:48,970
How could you cry like that
during his test? You're his mom.

184
00:09:49,376 --> 00:09:50,684
Exactly.

185
00:09:51,372 --> 00:09:54,836
She didn't like the smaller rooms,
so she paid for a private room.

186
00:09:54,928 --> 00:09:57,439
Good for you. You really look rich.

187
00:09:58,928 --> 00:10:00,932
Dad said I did the right thing too.

188
00:10:05,928 --> 00:10:07,484
Everything's going to be okay.

189
00:10:08,306 --> 00:10:10,343
Mom, you should go.

190
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:12,851
We'll run the tests and call you.

191
00:10:13,436 --> 00:10:14,436
Okay.

192
00:10:16,296 --> 00:10:18,680
Don't let Mai watch
when they do the bone marrow test.

193
00:10:18,724 --> 00:10:20,588
- You handle everything.
- Of course.

194
00:10:31,724 --> 00:10:33,046
Honey.

195
00:10:34,688 --> 00:10:36,556
I'm scared.

196
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:40,731
Again? Mom told you not to do this.

197
00:10:41,772 --> 00:10:44,765
Mom, why are you crying? Go to a club.

198
00:10:45,588 --> 00:10:46,588
You're right.

199
00:10:46,990 --> 00:10:49,796
Your mom loves going clubbing,
so maybe I should send her out.

200
00:10:59,316 --> 00:11:01,492
My baby.

201
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:19,491
Again. Fix your posture.
Your bow hold is wrong.

202
00:11:19,529 --> 00:11:22,486
For the entrance exam, precision
comes first. The music comes after.

203
00:11:22,935 --> 00:11:25,563
Don't let the notes drop,
and don't lose the rhythm.

204
00:11:25,565 --> 00:11:26,964
One, two, three.

205
00:11:27,428 --> 00:11:28,904
Two, two, three.

206
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:51,055
Okay, good. That's enough for today.

207
00:11:51,416 --> 00:11:54,664
You did well. Practice exactly
like you just did 20 more times.

208
00:11:54,732 --> 00:11:56,600
And on the 20th time,

209
00:11:56,602 --> 00:11:58,002
record it and send it to me.
I'll check it.

210
00:11:58,728 --> 00:12:00,023
Mrs. Na.

211
00:12:01,392 --> 00:12:03,395
Mom has something to tell you.

212
00:12:04,212 --> 00:12:05,212
Okay.

213
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:10,017
Yes, ma'am. How have you been?

214
00:12:11,504 --> 00:12:12,907
"His mistress?"

215
00:12:12,910 --> 00:12:14,513
Watch your words.

216
00:12:14,656 --> 00:12:17,325
I was his wife in every way for 30 years.

217
00:12:17,328 --> 00:12:18,500
Anyway,

218
00:12:18,900 --> 00:12:20,929
if you're uncomfortable, then stop.

219
00:12:20,932 --> 00:12:24,003
Is she taking cello lessons
or lessons on married life?

220
00:12:28,428 --> 00:12:32,506
Fine. I've heard enough nonsense.

221
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,757
Yes. I understand.

222
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:41,105
Find a teacher with a spotless reputation
and have her teach properly.

223
00:12:41,656 --> 00:12:42,656
Yes.

224
00:12:43,648 --> 00:12:44,648
What?

225
00:12:44,880 --> 00:12:46,836
You keep nagging more and more.

226
00:12:46,856 --> 00:12:48,688
- Dad's gone, so you look down on me?
- Mom.

227
00:12:54,360 --> 00:12:56,284
I'm sorry it has to end like this.

228
00:12:57,090 --> 00:12:59,667
Go. Work hard
and get into an arts high school.

229
00:12:59,669 --> 00:13:01,150
I'll be cheering for you.

230
00:13:01,608 --> 00:13:03,812
- Yes.
- Yeah.

231
00:13:09,644 --> 00:13:11,724
Seriously. How disgusting!

232
00:13:11,890 --> 00:13:14,508
She said she'd find someone
with a clean past and send her over.

233
00:13:15,070 --> 00:13:17,364
Why did you let her go on for so long?
You should've hung up.

234
00:13:19,576 --> 00:13:20,880
Want some coffee?

235
00:13:22,068 --> 00:13:23,204
Yeah.

236
00:13:24,430 --> 00:13:26,665
Do we have enough
for this month's expenses?

237
00:13:26,668 --> 00:13:28,272
We have enough for that.

238
00:13:29,096 --> 00:13:30,669
I got my severance pay.

239
00:13:31,332 --> 00:13:33,337
The problem is paying for the jewelry
from that damn family.

240
00:13:33,340 --> 00:13:35,417
You said you split it into 36 months.

241
00:13:35,441 --> 00:13:37,998
Yeah. Thanks.

242
00:13:39,792 --> 00:13:42,861
I'll go if the publishing company
gets back to me.

243
00:13:43,169 --> 00:13:44,948
But you said the bathroom was dirty.

244
00:13:45,680 --> 00:13:47,484
I just won't use the bathroom. It's fine.

245
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:58,836
Every time we clear one hurdle,
another one appears.

246
00:14:00,190 --> 00:14:02,784
This is all because of you.

247
00:14:11,492 --> 00:14:14,640
Ask at the café.
See if there's a part-time job for me too.

248
00:14:17,092 --> 00:14:22,440
I think I understand now
why you kept the rumors from spreading.

249
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:24,186
When I was young,

250
00:14:24,676 --> 00:14:28,436
I thought things would've been fine
if you hadn't kept it a secret.

251
00:14:28,968 --> 00:14:31,360
I thought it was all your fault.

252
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,252
I'm sorry.

253
00:14:34,304 --> 00:14:35,736
I only thought about myself.

254
00:14:36,810 --> 00:14:39,393
What parent doesn't want
to brag about their child?

255
00:14:40,030 --> 00:14:41,560
A beautiful daughter like you,

256
00:14:42,192 --> 00:14:43,711
I wanted to show you off too.

257
00:14:43,752 --> 00:14:46,125
What's gotten into you?
You're actually complimenting me.

258
00:14:46,128 --> 00:14:47,776
Your dad isn't around anymore.

259
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:51,612
Since he always praised you,
I ended up holding back.

260
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:57,495
Live long enough to understand how I feel.

261
00:15:08,520 --> 00:15:10,174
This is Ugly Publishing Company.

262
00:15:10,669 --> 00:15:13,918
We regret to inform you that
you were not selected for this position.

263
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:15,396
Unbelievable!

264
00:15:15,748 --> 00:15:17,793
I was ready to take the job,
and they rejected me?

265
00:15:20,607 --> 00:15:22,195
I'm so pissed off.

266
00:15:22,197 --> 00:15:24,597
You'd hesitate even if they begged you.
How dare they reject you?

267
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:27,103
Thanks for getting angry
on my behalf, my friend.

268
00:15:27,192 --> 00:15:30,137
I'm so stunned I can't even get angry.
I'm just numb.

269
00:15:31,528 --> 00:15:32,940
Text them right now.

270
00:15:33,010 --> 00:15:34,270
"Even if you ask me to come, I won't."

271
00:15:34,324 --> 00:15:37,277
And be sure to add,
"You should clean your bathroom."

272
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:42,023
I'm really starting to understand
how hard it is to find a job.

273
00:15:42,044 --> 00:15:45,022
Cheer up.
There's a place for you somewhere.

274
00:15:50,040 --> 00:15:51,400
The boss wants to see you.

275
00:15:52,068 --> 00:15:53,398
He wants you to come down with me.

276
00:15:54,108 --> 00:15:55,108
Me?

277
00:15:56,424 --> 00:15:59,258
Perfect timing. This is amazing.

278
00:15:59,364 --> 00:16:01,602
I got chills just now.

279
00:16:01,848 --> 00:16:03,440
Why? What's wrong?

280
00:16:03,516 --> 00:16:05,920
She's been interviewing for jobs
at publishing companies.

281
00:16:06,012 --> 00:16:07,156
Really?

282
00:16:07,764 --> 00:16:08,996
That's great.

283
00:16:09,488 --> 00:16:11,840
- Let's do this together.
- Sounds good.

284
00:16:13,169 --> 00:16:14,500
Delivery!

285
00:16:16,752 --> 00:16:19,019
Excuse me. What is all this...

286
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:23,344
- Did you order this?
- No.

287
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,127
There's a lot.

288
00:16:30,400 --> 00:16:32,212
This is from Ji Hu.

289
00:16:32,590 --> 00:16:35,364
- He sent all this for us to share.
- Why would he?

290
00:16:35,367 --> 00:16:38,237
I told him I'd talk to you,
and he told me to do my best.

291
00:16:38,239 --> 00:16:39,347
He's trying to flatter us.

292
00:16:39,600 --> 00:16:42,920
His dad's the owner
of that publishing company.

293
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:46,124
- What?
- So I'll come up with the ideas,

294
00:16:46,168 --> 00:16:48,801
you'll draw, and his dad will fund it.

295
00:16:50,148 --> 00:16:52,524
It feels like you're getting
a free ride here, Boss.

296
00:16:52,576 --> 00:16:56,021
I told you to stop that habit
of pointing things out so directly.

297
00:16:56,585 --> 00:16:58,616
- Try dipping it.
- Okay.

298
00:16:59,288 --> 00:17:02,276
But I think I'll need some time
to think about it.

299
00:17:02,470 --> 00:17:05,074
Working with you sounds great,
but that man is...

300
00:17:05,460 --> 00:17:06,612
Trust me.

301
00:17:06,656 --> 00:17:08,952
His dad's a really good person.

302
00:17:09,064 --> 00:17:11,644
He has his own life.
He's separate from us.

303
00:17:11,676 --> 00:17:13,480
Do you really get to be picky right now?

304
00:17:13,536 --> 00:17:16,252
Even Sim Cheong threw herself
into the Indang Sea for her father.

305
00:17:16,330 --> 00:17:17,768
And you can't even endure this?

306
00:17:18,372 --> 00:17:21,578
What happened to my friend Na Ji Ni
who used to worry about her mom?

307
00:17:21,964 --> 00:17:23,533
Fine, stop.

308
00:17:23,576 --> 00:17:25,732
- Think about it while you eat.
- Okay.

309
00:17:25,870 --> 00:17:27,472
You still have time.

310
00:17:30,784 --> 00:17:31,908
It's good.

311
00:17:45,372 --> 00:17:47,798
Mom, the tests are done.

312
00:17:50,064 --> 00:17:52,241
O Reum cried so much he even fainted.

313
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:55,663
Honestly, just seeing the needle
made me feel like I'd faint too.

314
00:19:11,256 --> 00:19:14,227
How can you already be this worn out
just from the tests?

315
00:19:15,056 --> 00:19:17,426
What will you do
if it actually gets confirmed?

316
00:19:18,910 --> 00:19:21,670
I can't even imagine that.

317
00:19:22,432 --> 00:19:24,076
I'd rather die instead.

318
00:19:24,136 --> 00:19:26,151
You won't be able to endure anything
with that mindset.

319
00:19:27,424 --> 00:19:28,812
Sa Bin...

320
00:19:32,232 --> 00:19:33,336
Please get up.

321
00:19:33,864 --> 00:19:35,471
Today, instead of tone-deafness treatment,

322
00:19:35,684 --> 00:19:38,040
I'll treat your "life-deafness."

323
00:19:38,248 --> 00:19:39,419
"Life-deafness,"

324
00:19:39,790 --> 00:19:41,516
that's a term you came up with.

325
00:19:41,830 --> 00:19:44,619
If you can't live your life properly,
you're "life-deaf," right?

326
00:19:46,889 --> 00:19:48,340
Yes, that's right.

327
00:19:48,773 --> 00:19:51,940
Worrying about sorrow that hasn't come
is also "life-deafness."

328
00:19:55,565 --> 00:19:57,440
Now, repeat after me.

329
00:19:57,606 --> 00:19:58,962
"O Reum, stay strong."

330
00:20:00,617 --> 00:20:01,784
Come on.

331
00:20:04,440 --> 00:20:05,887
"O Reum, stay strong."

332
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:08,565
Good job. Cheers, ta-da!

333
00:20:13,690 --> 00:20:14,992
That's refreshing.

334
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:18,271
Please don't worry too much.

335
00:20:18,273 --> 00:20:21,880
O Reum will live long enough
to have chicken and beer with his grandma.

336
00:20:22,773 --> 00:20:24,492
Just thinking about it makes me happy.

337
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:30,479
Thank you. I'll stay strong.

338
00:20:30,481 --> 00:20:33,240
Yes, and even if it's confirmed,

339
00:20:33,458 --> 00:20:34,812
these days, it's highly treatable.

340
00:20:34,815 --> 00:20:36,523
The medical treatment is really advanced.

341
00:20:38,856 --> 00:20:40,218
I have to stay hopeful.

342
00:20:40,898 --> 00:20:42,315
(My Musician)

343
00:20:44,106 --> 00:20:45,354
Pick up.

344
00:20:45,356 --> 00:20:47,794
Yes, excuse me for a moment.

345
00:20:53,398 --> 00:20:54,606
Hello, it's me.

346
00:20:55,828 --> 00:20:56,994
Right now?

347
00:20:57,648 --> 00:20:59,251
Right now is a bit...

348
00:21:02,403 --> 00:21:05,115
I'm with a teacher I know,

349
00:21:05,481 --> 00:21:06,860
so I'm sorry.

350
00:21:06,940 --> 00:21:09,628
It's okay. I didn't tell you in advance.

351
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:12,149
But it's a bit strange.

352
00:21:14,194 --> 00:21:17,260
This is the first time
you've refused my request.

353
00:21:18,484 --> 00:21:19,895
Just saying.

354
00:21:19,940 --> 00:21:22,563
You're with your teacher,
so I'll let you go.

355
00:21:22,565 --> 00:21:24,252
It'd be rude if we talked too long.

356
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:27,153
I'm going to stay
and have a bit more to drink.

357
00:21:28,481 --> 00:21:29,938
Okay. See you next time.

358
00:21:29,940 --> 00:21:31,773
Yes, get home safely.

359
00:21:37,203 --> 00:21:38,994
I'm sorry.

360
00:21:59,315 --> 00:22:01,190
(Don't pick up)

361
00:22:02,231 --> 00:22:03,606
Go ahead and answer it.

362
00:22:04,023 --> 00:22:05,315
I don't have to.

363
00:22:26,065 --> 00:22:27,273
O Reum.

364
00:22:28,106 --> 00:22:30,815
O Reum, your uncle is here.

365
00:22:40,940 --> 00:22:43,016
Seung Woo, where are you?

366
00:22:43,023 --> 00:22:44,327
There's no one at home.

367
00:22:46,315 --> 00:22:47,523
Really?

368
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:50,080
Where are you? I'll come to you.

369
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:54,971
What can you do if you come?
Can you treat him or something?

370
00:22:55,315 --> 00:22:56,981
Seung Woo, what do you mean?

371
00:22:57,065 --> 00:22:58,479
What's wrong with O Reum?

372
00:22:58,481 --> 00:23:01,565
I came to get Mai's clothes
and some things needed for the hospital.

373
00:23:03,940 --> 00:23:05,581
They say it's not confirmed yet,

374
00:23:06,398 --> 00:23:08,027
but this is really hard to deal with.

375
00:23:10,731 --> 00:23:12,731
But where did mom go?

376
00:23:13,565 --> 00:23:15,634
She said she was heading home earlier.

377
00:23:17,023 --> 00:23:18,433
O Reum.

378
00:23:20,648 --> 00:23:22,396
- O Reum.
- Please be careful.

379
00:23:22,398 --> 00:23:24,731
- Mom.
- Move.

380
00:23:25,148 --> 00:23:27,562
I hate you.
I can't even stand the sight of you.

381
00:23:27,606 --> 00:23:29,979
Get out. You're just like your father.

382
00:23:30,103 --> 00:23:31,430
I really hate you.

383
00:23:31,523 --> 00:23:32,731
Mom.

384
00:23:34,273 --> 00:23:35,817
My eldest son.

385
00:23:36,856 --> 00:23:38,696
The son who's been like a husband to me.

386
00:23:40,273 --> 00:23:41,481
Sa Bin.

387
00:23:42,148 --> 00:23:43,646
I made my eldest son...

388
00:23:43,648 --> 00:23:45,981
cry so much.

389
00:23:47,065 --> 00:23:48,616
My eldest son...

390
00:23:48,981 --> 00:23:50,626
shouldn't have to cry anymore.

391
00:23:51,648 --> 00:23:53,394
He deserves to be happy.

392
00:23:54,953 --> 00:23:56,646
Yes.

393
00:23:56,648 --> 00:23:57,856
Don't worry.

394
00:23:58,398 --> 00:23:59,787
Nothing will happen...

395
00:24:00,311 --> 00:24:02,154
to our dear O Reum.

396
00:24:03,856 --> 00:24:07,621
This doctor of Korean medicine
is truly excellent,

397
00:24:07,773 --> 00:24:09,231
and he said O Reum will be fine.

398
00:24:09,315 --> 00:24:10,773
Well...

399
00:24:12,022 --> 00:24:13,157
Say hello.

400
00:24:13,731 --> 00:24:16,036
This is the doctor who prescribed
O Reum's herbal medicine.

401
00:24:16,231 --> 00:24:19,114
He gets tone-deafness treatment from me,

402
00:24:19,409 --> 00:24:23,423
and I get "life-deafness" treatment.

403
00:24:27,346 --> 00:24:29,438
I'm sorry.

404
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:31,312
She suddenly got drunk.

405
00:24:31,356 --> 00:24:32,938
Of course she got drunk suddenly.

406
00:24:32,940 --> 00:24:34,523
Do people get a preview
before they get drunk?

407
00:24:34,648 --> 00:24:35,856
Seung Woo.

408
00:24:40,690 --> 00:24:43,141
That rude brat...

409
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:46,648
Sa Bin.

410
00:24:47,398 --> 00:24:48,479
Thank you.

411
00:24:48,481 --> 00:24:49,873
You can go now.

412
00:24:50,231 --> 00:24:52,692
Yes, please get some rest.

413
00:25:09,231 --> 00:25:12,065
- How is O Reum?
- I saw him fall asleep after crying.

414
00:25:13,116 --> 00:25:14,848
I'll pack Mai's clothes...

415
00:25:14,856 --> 00:25:16,023
and head back.

416
00:25:16,398 --> 00:25:18,648
Okay, good job.

417
00:25:48,106 --> 00:25:49,940
You're going to become an alcoholic.

418
00:25:50,023 --> 00:25:51,781
What did you do to deserve a drink?

419
00:25:53,065 --> 00:25:55,722
- Yeong Ju.
- Don't even call my name.

420
00:25:56,034 --> 00:25:57,333
I'm so sick of the Chas.

421
00:25:57,789 --> 00:26:00,079
Love? Don't make me laugh.

422
00:26:00,190 --> 00:26:02,190
I can't even stand the sight of you,
you jerk.

423
00:26:02,356 --> 00:26:04,479
If I catch you seeing
that woman one more time,

424
00:26:04,481 --> 00:26:06,065
you're dead.

425
00:26:28,731 --> 00:26:30,106
My eldest son.

426
00:26:30,398 --> 00:26:32,129
My son who's like my husband.

427
00:26:32,762 --> 00:26:38,128
Sa Bin, I made my eldest son
cry so much.

428
00:26:44,565 --> 00:26:45,646
Mrs. Na.

429
00:26:45,648 --> 00:26:48,315
I felt bad leaving you to drink alone.

430
00:26:48,481 --> 00:26:49,731
I'm sorry.

431
00:26:49,815 --> 00:26:51,356
Let's drink together next time.

432
00:26:56,106 --> 00:26:58,396
Mrs. No, when you wake up in the morning,

433
00:26:58,398 --> 00:27:00,438
take what I put in your bag.

434
00:27:00,440 --> 00:27:02,479
Your hangover will go away quickly.

435
00:27:02,481 --> 00:27:05,731
And when O Reum's results come out,
please let me know.

436
00:27:05,940 --> 00:27:08,356
I'll help with whatever I can.

437
00:27:08,606 --> 00:27:09,967
From Im Sa Bin.

438
00:27:18,148 --> 00:27:20,315
(Haemyeong University Hospital)

439
00:27:23,315 --> 00:27:24,585
I'm sorry.

440
00:27:25,940 --> 00:27:28,356
It's an acute blood cancer in children.

441
00:27:34,981 --> 00:27:36,190
Mai...

442
00:27:53,106 --> 00:27:56,356
(Family Register)

443
00:27:56,606 --> 00:27:58,148
Is O Reum sick?

444
00:27:58,190 --> 00:27:59,521
- Mom.
- Did you forget?

445
00:27:59,523 --> 00:28:01,291
His mother chased us all the way here...

446
00:28:01,294 --> 00:28:02,396
to take this house.

447
00:28:02,398 --> 00:28:04,749
- That's why her kid turned out like that.
- Mom.

448
00:28:04,752 --> 00:28:06,481
I decided to take over your dad's company.

449
00:28:06,523 --> 00:28:09,560
- How about investing more in Indonesia?
- More than this?

450
00:28:09,563 --> 00:28:11,479
Why are you two coming in together
this morning?

451
00:28:11,481 --> 00:28:13,731
Why on earth are you meeting Na Ji Ni
this early?

452
00:28:13,773 --> 00:28:17,059
- You're the one cheating, aren't you?
- Do Do Hee, why did you lie?

453
00:28:18,483 --> 00:28:20,483
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)

